            <p class="mb-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-700">That’s why even after everything has ended, your mind doesn’t simply accept it as “over,” instead it keeps pulling you back into moments that once felt good—like their messages, their voice, the way they made you feel seen—because your brain is wired to hold onto emotional highs, almost like an addiction pattern, where it keeps searching for what once gave it comfort, even if that same thing is no longer available in reality.</p>

